From 149a2ae6e6ca8190c78e256a8cb79169ae67da64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 11:53:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/26] arm64: dts: rk3566-pinetab2: force the OTG port to
 peripheral

The USB gadget never enumerates on the charging/OTG port. Reading dwc3's own
registers shows why - the D+ pullup is simply never asserted:

    /sys/kernel/debug/usb/fcc00000.usb/mode       = device
    /sys/kernel/debug/usb/fcc00000.usb/link_state = SS.Disabled
    GCTL = 0x30c12004      (PRTCAPDIR = 2, device)
    DCTL = 0x00f00000      (bit31 RUN_STOP = 0)

so the controller is correctly in device mode with a bound gadget
(configfs g1, ecm.usb0, UDC = fcc00000.usb) and a live cable - Type-C
resolves, the port sinks 450mA from the host, extcon reports USB=1 - and the
host still sees nothing at all, because nothing is pulling D+ up for it to
detect.

dwc3_gadget_pullup() in this tree withholds the pullup in OTG mode:

    if (is_on && dwc->dr_mode == USB_DR_MODE_OTG && !dwc->current_dr_connected)
            return 0;

current_dr_connected is only ever cleared by the role-switch or extcon paths
in drd.c; this node has neither an extcon property nor (after this patch) a
role switch, so in principle it keeps its "true" default. Whatever leaves it
clear in practice, dr_mode = "peripheral" removes the question: the OTG test
is false by construction and the pullup follows the gadget binding.

That is also what this port is for. The tablet has a second, dedicated host
controller (fd000000.usb, usb_host1_xhci, with its own EHCI/OHCI companions)
for peripherals, so nothing is lost by making this one device-only. Charging
is unaffected - it is negotiated over CC by the RT1711H and does not involve
dwc3's role at all.

The connector's OF-graph port to dwc3 goes with the role switch, as it would
otherwise dangle.

Tested: with only the role switch removed (and dr_mode left at the SoC's
"otg") the gadget still did not enumerate and RUN_STOP stayed clear, which is
what prompted reading the register in the first place.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board configuration]
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
 .../boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi    | 21 +------------------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 20 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi
index 05429c0be046..5fde8afb13fb 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi
@@ -1001,14 +1001,8 @@ &usb_host0_ohci {
 
 /* OTG port controller */
 &usb_host0_xhci {
-	usb-role-switch;
+	dr_mode = "peripheral";
 	status = "okay";
-
-	port {
-		usb_host0_xhci_typec_hs: endpoint {
-			remote-endpoint = <&typec_hs_usb_host0_xhci>;
-		};
-	};
 };
 
 &usb_host1_xhci {
@@ -1082,19 +1076,6 @@ connector {
 			op-sink-microwatt = <2500000>;
 			sink-pdos = <PDO_FIXED(5000, 3000, PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM)>;
 			source-pdos = <PDO_FIXED(5000, 500, PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM)>;
-
-			ports {
-				#address-cells = <1>;
-				#size-cells = <0>;
-
-				port@0 {
-					reg = <0>;
-
-					typec_hs_usb_host0_xhci: endpoint {
-						remote-endpoint = <&usb_host0_xhci_typec_hs>;
-					};
-				};
-			};
 		};
 	};
 };
